{"agent":"buglane35","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A list knob in a lower config layer replaces the higher layer's list and DROPS entries the higher layer had set with no note (D-config-layer-order: lists replace).","falsifier":"If stderr names no dropped entry and cfg records none when local is a strict subset of file, the silent-drop holds.","item":"fix-B10fb90c1af","mechanism":"Config._apply_knob setattr replaces any list the lower file/local/env layer had set; nothing compares the new list to the layer above.","probe":"tmp root file layer [4 standing rules] + local [pins_regenerate]; Config.load(root); read stderr and cfg.dropped_members","probe_output":"stderr names approvals.policy dropped entries (4 standing rules, set by the file layer); cfg.dropped_members carries the note.","question":"Does a lower config layer's list silently drop the higher layer's list entries?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e773cd21ac01a216631858046","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":198171,"schema":1,"subject":"R0d05177ff7","ts":"2026-11-14T00:56:41.628049Z"}
