{"agent":"buglane35","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_dropped_list_entries` accepts arbitrary list entries and its docstring explicitly says the elements “need not be hashable,” but `_note_dropped` joins the returned raw entries with `', '.join(dropped)`, which requires every entry to be a `str`. Given a list knob whose dropped entries are not strings (for example the unhashable list entries the docstring allows: `below = [[1], [2]]`, `value = []`), `_dropped_list_entries` returns `[[1], [2]]` and `_note_dropped` raises `TypeError: sequence item 0: expected str instance, list found` during config load instead of recording the intended note.","digest":"19463f0932da3833","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/config/_core.py:_note_dropped","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/config/_core.py:_note_dropped"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The warn-once memo is keyed by the knob name before the first colon, not by the actual dropped entries. In a long-running ddflow process that reloads config (the docstring itself mentions MCP replies, so a server/daemon is plausible), the first load that drops `skip_after_unavailable`, `complete_unavailable`, and `claim_unavailable` adds `(root, \"approvals.policy\")` to `_WARNED_DROPPED`. If the operator then edits the local layer so it instead drops `complete_unavailable`/`claim_unavailable` but keeps `skip_after_unavailable`, the next `Config.load` will have those new dropped entries in `cfg.dropped_members`, but `_warn_dropped` will suppress the stderr note because the same key was already warned. The newly loosened entries are then silent at load, contrary to r-tighten-only: a lower layer may tighten, never silently loosen.","digest":"8e573c1f1e956a6e","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/config/_warn.py:_warn_dropped","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/config/_warn.py:_warn_dropped"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":9918,"diff_sha":"b0a41cf3b9a66051e4019bae5bf2b2dd852b47734cdd39eaa055f8e6070807c5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B10fb90c1af","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":301.5,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"66aabdfd482fee79","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B10fb90c1af.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261114T005805Z-773a8b16.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"ae4c8a7e5daf541be688c6568c798e38ef7df0d6","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/config/_core.py":"100644 91325efcadd393156640c1b1e7b4ca50448a666c","ddflow/config/_warn.py":"100644 6574275de5195b340bf677f9ea373611e33b3901","ddflow/services/configcompat.py":"100644 d84a04b83aecfc8605ff2a797551cabeb06582c4","tests/test_config_layers.py":"100644 3fef9dad10c1662dd73076e1d670986ae7a416b9"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/config/_core.py:_note_dropped","ddflow/config/_warn.py:_warn_dropped"],"tree_sha":"ae4c8a7e5daf+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"eee3567e8538527d638617180","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":198233,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B10fb90c1af","ts":"2026-11-14T01:03:11.026954Z"}
